#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""soteria — supervisor layer for coding agents. Stdlib only.

Soteria supervises; it does not sandbox by itself. Enforcement is delegated
per platform: Seatbelt kernel box on macOS, soft box elsewhere, Docker
container boundary, or delegated nono engine (--backend nono, the Linux
kernel story). Per-tool policy is enforced by a supervised broker: shims
forward to a host-side daemon that re-gates and spawns each tool under its
own Seatbelt profile (fs_read/fs_write via
command_policies.commands.<tool>.sandbox) plus resource caps
(--memory/--max-processes/--tool-timeout).
  - jail cwd to one project dir (child runs with cwd=project)
  - composable JSON profiles (minimal/developer/claude-code/codex) + groups
  - scrub real secrets from child env, phantom placeholders + localhost
    reverse-proxy injection with endpoint rules + deny/always-denied hosts
  - argv + tool gate: denylist + deny-only tools + argv allow-lists
    (gh view, git no --force), direct-exec bypass deny, ask on irreversible
  - pre/post snapshot + diff + verify + cleanup + one-command undo
  - hash-chained NDJSON audit (logs --verify) with redaction
  - why --path/--host/--command explainability, profile init/validate/show/diff

Fails closed on deny; ask defaults to deny on timeout/EOF.
Shims mediate PATH lookups only (builtins/absolute paths/in-interpreter
calls bypass them); the kernel box is the real wall. See docs/THREAT_MODEL.md.

Usage:
  ./soteria setup                   # host check + install presets
  ./soteria launch
  ./soteria run --allow ./proj --network-profile developer --credential github --rollback -- <cmd...>
  ./soteria list | ./soteria show <id> [--diff] | ./soteria verify <id> | ./soteria undo <id> [--yes]
  ./soteria cleanup --keep 10 [--dry-run] | ./soteria logs [--limit N] [-f] [--verify]
  ./soteria scan [--session ID] [--json] | ./soteria timeline [ID]
  ./soteria profile list|init|validate|show|diff | ./soteria why --path P | --host H | --command CMD...
Freeze to native exe: `pip install pyinstaller && pyinstaller --clean --noconfirm soteria.spec`  # spec, not script
(profiles/ + ui/ bundled via soteria.spec).
"""
